{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggEwdeQfqwccJgDB3hZc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the groszes add up to the total again.\n\nThe bug was in `money.py`. It gave everyone `total // people` and dropped the remainder. It now uses `divmod` and gives one extra grosz to each of the first `remainder` people.\n\nI added two tests to `test_money.py` and watched both fail before the fix:\n- **Exact case:** `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`.\n- **Sum check:** the shares add up to the total for every total from 0 to 49 and 1 to 7 people.\n\nAll 5 tests pass. I didn't run a linter or build, and the repo has no config for either.\n\nEarlier people get the extra grosz, so the order is deterministic. If you want it assigned differently, for example to whoever paid, that would be a separate change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":20602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":657},"output_tokens":284,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f111ff59-582d-4c54-8471-7e0b776ef2e1","uuid":"36caaa73-9a79-483d-bf53-34acab941ac9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:35:58.790Z","request_id":"req_011CggEwdQGmF8rygWTAEZAU"}
